\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Overview
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Enngraff is a fictional engraving studio working in the Cyber Sigilism style: fine, branching sigil lines burned into metal, glass, wood and everyday devices. The project covered the full path from brand concept to live website. I defined the brand (naming, value proposition, audience, tone, palette and typography), built a design system in Figma, and handed it over to Figma Make, an agentic AI tool, which built a four-page website (Home, Services, Detail and Contact) from my tokens and written specifications alone.\

\f0\b Title: Studio Engramm\
Categorie: Webdevelopment and Branding\
Problem
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Figma Make never sees the design. It only receives text: tokens, component specs and a single prompt for the Home page. The brand made this harder. Cyber Sigilism lives on detailed ornament, blackletter type and glowing effects, which are almost impossible to describe precisely in words. At the same time, the original design still had gaps that would have carried straight into the build: hardcoded colours, variables named by appearance instead of role, missing component states, and placeholder text.\

\f0\b Solution
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 I separated what an AI can rebuild from text from what it can\'92t. The layout stayed clean and structural, while the ornamental parts became assets: the 13-point star CTA was exported as an SVG with a 
\f2\fs26 currentColor
\f1\fs24  fill, and its glow became its own effect token. I restructured the Figma file into a role-based system with nine colour variables, a seven-step spacing scale, six text styles on Google Fonts, and seven components with declared variants. All of it was compiled into a Token Sheet and cleaned JSON specs. Those became the only material Figma Make received, followed by one precise prompt for the Home.\

\f0\b Result
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 The result is a live multi-page website with working navigation, responsive layouts for desktop and mobile, and a contact form with visible states. The Home was generated in a single prompt and refined afterwards only by hand, through Point and Edit and the code editor. The remaining pages were built across documented correction rounds. The project also produced a reusable brand and token system that carries forward into Eval 03, and a clear lesson about agentic workflows: the output is only as good as the structure and language you hand over.\
Once your site is finished, I\'92d make the Result section more concrete with your actual outcomes, such as how closely the one-shot Home matched your Figma design, how many correction rounds you needed, and what you fixed by hand. Those specifics will make it much stronger. I can also set the four sections as a 1920\'d71080 slide in the same style as your other sheets.\
